"ex-positive-weighted-volume-on-an-open-interval","ex-density-measure-in-two-overlapping-circle-charts","ex-density-measure-on-a-nonorientable-manifold","ex-zero-dimensional-density-measure-is-weighted-counting","cex-a-smooth-density-can-have-infinite-total-mass","ex-borel-ball-volume-before-any-comparison-theorem"],"conventions":[{"convention":"Multi-indices use 0 in N, and coefficient majorisation compares ordinary Taylor coefficients, not unnormalised derivatives.","fixed_by":"def-real-analytic-germ-in-several-variables","matters_for":["def-coefficientwise-majorisation-of-multivariable-power-series","lem-coefficient-majorisation-is-preserved-by-sums-products-composition-and-differentiation","lem-an-analytic-germ-has-a-rational-geometric-majorant","thm-cauchy-kovalevskaya-for-first-order-analytic-systems-in-normal-form"]},{"convention":"The Cauchy–Kovalevskaya conclusions are local real-analytic germ statements; fully nonlinear equations are restricted to a selected compatible implicit branch.","fixed_by":"thm-cauchy-kovalevskaya-for-a-noncharacteristic-analytic-cauchy-problem","matters_for":["lem-analytic-noncharacteristic-hypersurfaces-flatten-to-a-coordinate-hyperplane","lem-higher-order-analytic-normal-form-reduces-to-a-first-order-system","cex-analytic-heat-data-can-have-divergent-time-taylor-series","rem-cauchy-kovalevskaya-is-an-analytic-not-smooth-well-posedness-theorem"]},{"convention":"Surface-measure results assume AC_omega; a bounded C1 domain is nonempty, bounded, open, locally a subgraph, and C1(overline Omega) means interior derivatives extend continuously to the closure.","fixed_by":"def-bounded-c-one-domain-boundary-charts-and-outward-normal","matters_for":["thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-c-one-euclidean-domains","cor-first-green-identity-on-a-bounded-c-one-domain","cor-second-green-identity-on-a-bounded-c-one-domain"]},{"convention":"Surface orientation is the actual exterior side: on a graph z=h(y) bounding the subgraph, nu dS=(-Dh,1)dy.","fixed_by":"lem-surface-integral-is-independent-of-c-one-boundary-charts","matters_for":["thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-c-one-euclidean-domains","thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-piecewise-c-one-domains","ex-surface-density-and-outward-normal-on-a-graph","cex-reversing-boundary-orientation-reverses-flux"]},{"convention":"A piecewise C1 domain means the stated finite presentation: compact faces, a compact surface-null edge set, faces counted once off that set, and outward normals on every exposed or hole face.","fixed_by":"def-bounded-piecewise-c-one-euclidean-domain","matters_for":["lem-surface-null-edges-admit-small-gradient-cutoffs","thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-piecewise-c-one-domains","ex-internal-face-cancellation-for-two-glued-regions","ex-punctured-domains-and-truncated-cones-with-explicit-faces"]},{"convention":"A nonnegative Borel density is pointwise chartwise Borel with the absolute-Jacobian transition law and 0 times infinity equal to 0; its Borel measure and its completion remain distinct domains.","fixed_by":"def-borel-measurable-nonnegative-density-on-a-manifold","matters_for":["lem-measurable-density-chart-integrals-agree-on-overlaps","thm-density-measure-is-independent-of-the-chart-gluing","thm-density-measure-integration-agrees-with-smooth-density-integration","ex-zero-dimensional-density-measure-is-weighted-counting"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"thm-cauchy-kovalevskaya-for-first-order-analytic-systems-in-normal-form","statement":"Let d,N>=1, let g be analytic near zero, and let F be analytic near (0,0,g(0),Dg(0)). Then u_t=F(t,x,u,D_xu), u(0,x)=g(x) has a unique real analytic solution germ at (0,0).","used_by":["lem-higher-order-analytic-normal-form-reduces-to-a-first-order-system","thm-cauchy-kovalevskaya-for-a-noncharacteristic-analytic-cauchy-problem","ex-cauchy-kovalevskaya-for-an-analytic-transport-equation"]},{"id":"lem-the-goursat-majorant-equation-has-a-convergent-positive-power-series-solution","statement":"The specified Goursat majorant equation has an analytic positive branch and yields a convergent positive majorant system with zero origin jet.","used_by":["thm-cauchy-kovalevskaya-for-first-order-analytic-systems-in-normal-form"]},{"id":"lem-higher-order-analytic-normal-form-reduces-to-a-first-order-system","statement":"The complete lower-jet first-order system has an analytic solution satisfying U_beta=D^beta U_0, and is equivalent to the scalar solved normal equation with its m data.","used_by":["thm-cauchy-kovalevskaya-for-a-noncharacteristic-analytic-cauchy-problem","ex-cauchy-kovalevskaya-for-a-second-order-normal-form"]},{"id":"lem-analytic-noncharacteristic-hypersurfaces-flatten-to-a-coordinate-hyperplane","statement":"Analytic noncharacteristic hypersurfaces flatten analytically; the transformed pure normal coefficient is the linearized principal symbol at dphi, and a nonzero value gives a local analytic solved branch.","used_by":["thm-cauchy-kovalevskaya-for-a-noncharacteristic-analytic-cauchy-problem"]},{"id":"lem-c-one-change-of-variables-for-nonnegative-borel-functions-via-radon-uniqueness","statement":"For a C1 diffeomorphism T:U->V of open Euclidean sets and nonnegative Borel h, integral_V h equals integral_U (h composed with T)|det DT|, as an extended nonnegative equality.","used_by":["lem-surface-integral-is-independent-of-c-one-boundary-charts","lem-euclidean-chart-measure-agrees-with-polar-surface-measure","lem-measurable-density-chart-integrals-agree-on-overlaps"]},{"id":"lem-surface-integral-is-independent-of-c-one-boundary-charts","statement":"The finite-chart Gram-density construction is a finite Borel surface measure independent of charts and partitions, with graph density sqrt(1+|Dh|^2) and the continuous exterior normal.","used_by":["thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-c-one-euclidean-domains","lem-surface-null-edges-admit-small-gradient-cutoffs","thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-piecewise-c-one-domains","lem-euclidean-chart-measure-agrees-with-polar-surface-measure"]},{"id":"lem-local-graph-flux-from-fubini-and-the-fundamental-theorem","statement":"For a compactly localized C1 field on a one-sided C1 graph cylinder, the volume divergence integral equals the graph flux; an interior compactly supported C1 field has zero divergence integral.","used_by":["thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-c-one-euclidean-domains","thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-piecewise-c-one-domains"]},{"id":"thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-c-one-euclidean-domains","statement":"For n>=2, a bounded C1 domain Omega and F in C1(overline Omega), integral_Omega div F equals integral_boundary Omega F dot nu dS, with both integrals finite.","used_by":["cor-first-green-identity-on-a-bounded-c-one-domain","ex-divergence-theorem-on-a-ball-in-rn","cex-reversing-boundary-orientation-reverses-flux"]},{"id":"thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-piecewise-c-one-domains","statement":"For the specified finite piecewise C1 presentation and F in C1(overline Omega), integral_Omega div F is the sum of the face fluxes, with shared-face fluxes cancelling in a specified finite gluing.","used_by":["cor-first-green-identity-on-a-bounded-c-one-domain","ex-internal-face-cancellation-for-two-glued-regions","ex-punctured-domains-and-truncated-cones-with-explicit-faces"]},{"id":"thm-density-measure-is-independent-of-the-chart-gluing","statement":"All chart-partition constructions give the same measure mu_r; if Borel E is contained in chart x, then mu_r(E)=integral_x(E) r_x d lambda_n.","used_by":["thm-a-positive-smooth-density-defines-a-locally-finite-radon-measure","thm-density-measure-integration-agrees-with-smooth-density-integration","ex-chart-gluing-recovers-euclidean-lebesgue-measure","ex-density-measure-in-two-overlapping-circle-charts"]},{"id":"thm-a-positive-smooth-density-defines-a-locally-finite-radon-measure","statement":"A finite-valued positive smooth density gives a compact-finite, locally finite, sigma-finite regular Borel measure, hence a Radon measure; its completion is not identified with its Borel domain.","used_by":["thm-density-measure-integration-agrees-with-smooth-density-integration","cor-positive-density-measures-assign-positive-volume-to-nonempty-open-sets-and-metric-balls","fs-local-finiteness-means-finite-total-density-measure","fs-orientation-is-required-for-a-density-measure"]},{"id":"thm-density-measure-integration-agrees-with-smooth-density-integration","statement":"Borel nonnegative and L1 density-measure integration has the stated chart formula, and for a positive smooth density it agrees with compactly supported smooth density integration.","used_by":["ex-positive-weighted-volume-on-an-open-interval","ex-density-measure-in-two-overlapping-circle-charts"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"def-countable-choice","used_for":"AC_omega convention for countable covers, measure and integration.","opened":true},{"id":"def-multivariable-power-series","used_for":"Multi-index series and absolute convergence.","opened":true},{"id":"def-real-analytic-function","used_for":"One-variable analytic comparison.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-power-series-define-holomorphic-functions-in-several-variables","used_for":"Complexification, coefficient bounds, and termwise differentiation.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-geometric-series","used_for":"Geometric and reciprocal series estimates.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-cauchy-estimates-on-a-polydisc","used_for":"Analytic geometric-majorant coefficient bound.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-holomorphic-inverse-function-theorem-several-variables","used_for":"Analytic inverse construction.","opened":true},{"id":"cor-uniqueness-of-multivariable-power-series-coefficients","used_for":"Coefficient uniqueness.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-power-series-expansion-in-several-complex-variables","used_for":"Holomorphic power-series expansions.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-symmetry-of-higher-mixed-partials","used_for":"Commutation of analytic mixed derivatives.","opened":true},{"id":"lem-principal-symbol-under-a-c-